          "tz": -300
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Oleg Drokin",
          "email": "green@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-11-06 02:14:19.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: speed up conf-sanity test_46a",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: speed up conf-sanity test_46a\n\ntest_46a calls reformat_and_config, which starts and stops the\nMDS and OST1 to generate the config logs, and then the test\nstarts the same targets again. Reformat and start them directly\ninstead: OST1 now registers on its first start, and OSTs 2..N\nstill register as additional OSTs, which is what the test\ncovers.\n\nThe wait for the additional OST imports ran one do_rpc_nodes\nper OST per MDT. Do one wait over all the new OSTs per MDS\nhost.\n\nMeasured on a single-node rocky9 ldiskfs VM with 2 MDTs and 3\nOSTs, test_46a took 77, 71 and 79 s before. After it took 124\n(first run after deploy), 49, 41, 42, 45 and 52 s. In CI the\ntest averages 572 s over 4473 runs per 30 days; the VM does\nnot show the slow per-call cost of do_rpc_nodes there, so the\nCI saving should be larger than the 30 s seen here.\n\n57373 (LU-14772) moves test_46a to another file and would need\na rebase over this.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=conf-sanity env=ONLY=46a\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ife2455fdd4fcf6bc98745e90f75f1a1e02f4bf84\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70194\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Alex Deiter <adeiter@ddn.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
